		<div class="post" id="post-1568438">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,1568438)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-1568438">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drewbear" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301632); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=301632&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973860" alt="Drewbear" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=301632)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drewbear" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301632); return false;" >Drewbear</a></span> <span class="odate time_1348073386 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Sep 2012 16:49</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1568438">
									

<p>Like I said, this was originally an orphaned supplement to a SCP that got deleted. I don't know what the original SCP was, but the way <em>this</em> supplement was worded made it seem much more like the entire plot of land was the SCP, rather than the goo stuff. I <em>vaguelly</em> remember a plot-of-land SCP where the first person who entered it gained total vocal control over any subsequent people who entered, and I think this might have been attached to that.</p>
<p>Anyway, I redirected the focus slightly to put the goo<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-142951-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-142951-1')">1</a></sup> as the SCP, with somewhat undefined properties. This interview is supposed to be taking place within the first week of the Foundation taking control of the location, so they wouldn't've been able to test it yet, and Smalls obviously had no idea either. Who knows? The &quot;recurrence&quot; might be an entirely unintended side effect that happens when you misuse the goo by eating it instead of washing your hair with it or something.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-142951-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-142951-1')">1</a>. Note that I never said it's food. Smalls just said they <em>used it</em> as food. After all, Play-doh is edible &amp; non-toxic, but isn't food.</div>
</div>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>Giving bearhugs to the unsuspecting since 1872.</p>

				</div>
					
